t and s-leader-loop-contiguous implement actual registration, count notification and successful response. These bodies support the four bindings without interpreting their guards as normative rules. Correlation: operation is independent identity shared across prerequisite/result events. The reply is physically held by entered/release channels. Election completion occurs before the public VerifyLeader call; the registration notification is consumed while the old heartbeat is still blocked. Prerequisite references link election to reply and admission to election; literals restrict the selected terms to 7 and 8, so the inequality cannot accidentally compare arbitrary unrelated epochs. There is one event sequence per operation. The result is independently measured from Future.Error, not assigned from election state. The completed filter selects an actual comparison; success itself is not filtered out. Shutdown is independent of the forbidden outcome: heartbeat stop precedes release, the worker finishes, and leader-loop shutdown follows a bounded Future.Error observation. The harness does not fabricate target replies or alter protocol code. Raw trace reaches all prerequisites and reports F Leader at term 8, N stored vote term 8, admission elected_term 8 and completed=true/success=true/calls=1. The configured assertion success=false therefore disagrees with the actual return, matching the runner checker result violated even though the Go test process passed. Alternative paths are retained: newer incoming RPC or ordinary response can force step-down and nil notifyCh prevents later votes; this schedule provides no newer reply to L and does not claim those protections fail in all histories. No issue found with the bounded result comparison and its conditional fixture scope; this review does not turn the assumed prefix into a reachability proof.'\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id=sid,rationale='Whole-artifact review of the accepted check and actual execution, with correspondence limited to the controlled fixture and explicit exclusions.',review_items=[dict(target_id=sid,aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=required+['s-heartbeat','s-follower-timeout','s-future-completion','s-append-completion'],rationale=rationale,counterevidence=[],limitations=limitations)],resolutions=[],feedback=dict(ref_ids=[sid,'cf548422b333468f8168df15d712e0d1'],answered='The accepted bounded checker compared the completed public Future.Error result against the negative authority condition after a correlated actual replacement election and reported violated. The saved trace shows success=true where the assertion requires false. This is a local conditional result, not a full-cluster reproduction.',remaining=limitations,understanding='unchanged',rationale='The accepted fact remains counted verification support; no execution-specific outcome is promoted into a general Fact. The next discriminating research decision is a constructor-initialized three-node history with ordinary replication workers controlled through transport delay, retaining the same pre-produced reply and public completion endpoint. That would address initial-prefix and omitted-worker reachability rather than repeat the local comparison.'))\njsonschema.validate(s,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\nPath('submission.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
